{"n": 648, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "648.webp", "text": "2834041\n\n2834042\n\n2834043\n\n34-8a\n\n3421812 OVERHAULING REAR BRAKE\nCALIPER\n— Use Repair Kit —\n\nRemove rear brake caliper — 34 21 220\nPress off plastic caps (1).\nUnscrew guide bolts (2).\n\nDisassemble caliper.\n\nRemove brake pads.\n\nInstallation:\n\nPress brake pad toward outside fully prior to\ninstalling spring (4).\n\nPress off rubber cap and clamping ring.\n\nPlace a liner (hard wood, hard felt or similar\nmaterial) in caliper recess to protect piston.\nPress out piston with compressed air applied\nthrough connection bore.\n\nCautiont\n\n10 bar (140 psi) air pressure is equal to a force\nof about 1250 N (275 Ibs.).\n\nCheck guide sleeves (5), using guide sleeves in\nrepair kit if necessary.\n\n2634044\n\n2834045\n\n- 7824046\n\nRemove seal coretully with a plastic needle\nClean cylinder bores and parts with alcohol\n\nand dry with compressed aw\n\nInspect cylinder bore, piston end flange surfaces\nfor damage thoroughly.\n\nMachining of cylinder bores and pistons is not\napproved.\n\nfastallavon\n\nGive all parts a light coat of ATE brake cylinder\npaste before installing\n\nPull rubber cap on to piston first\nDo not cant piston\nPress in piston with a piece of hard wood.\n\nPull rubber cap over edge of cylinder bore and\nsecure with clamping ring\nAssemble caliper", "words": [["2834041", 0.1976, 0.5, 0.2437, 0.5106], ["2834042", 0.1925, 0.7361, 0.2411, 0.7454], ["2834043", 0.191, 0.9695, 0.2381, 0.9781], ["34-8a", 0.4645, 0.0332, 0.5299, 0.0531], ["3421812", 0.2589, 0.0597, 0.308, 0.0703], ["OVERHAULING", 0.3212, 0.0597, 0.4037, 0.0703], ["REAR", 0.4083, 0.0597, 0.4377, 0.0703], ["BRAKE", 0.4422, 0.0603, 0.4797, 0.0703], ["CALIPER", 0.3212, 0.0756, 0.3678, 0.0869], ["—", 0.3222, 0.0975, 0.3283, 0.0995], ["Use", 0.3323, 0.0928, 0.349, 0.1028], ["Repair", 0.3526, 0.0915, 0.3835, 0.1048], ["Kit", 0.388, 0.0922, 0.4017, 0.1021], ["—", 0.4068, 0.0975, 0.4124, 0.0995], ["Remove", 0.2594, 0.1247,